0.6.0
  - Mesa 26.2.6 series: upstream's stable series at 4199d5b5c5b5, which
    was still keyed for 26.2.5 upstream. Beyond the 26.2.5 series it adds
    the DirectMesh auto-IDX/RDNA1 release and the 32-bit IDX setup args
    pad; the FSR4 patches are unchanged apart from their index lines.
    Verified before vendoring: the whole build order (series, local patch,
    OGC patches) applies cleanly to the pristine Mesa 26.2.6 tarball, and
    the key-bit files are byte-identical between 26.2.5 and 26.2.6.

0.5.0
  - The vendored series is keyed by the Mesa release it was rebased for.
    Mesa 26.2.5 spends one of the padding bits the BC-250 series funds its
    shader key flags from, so the series for 26.2.4 does not apply to 26.2.5
    and the other way round. The build picks the series that matches the
    base image's Mesa and fails when there is none.
  - Mesa 26.2.5 series: upstream commit "fund DirectMesh's key bits for
    26.2.5", which names the leftover key bits, moves the route-key mirrors
    to 28 bytes and bumps RADV_BC250_PIPELINE_PLAN_VERSION to 9.
  - The OpenGamingCollective patches are applied with one line of context
    dropped when the strict application fails, because OGC re-tags the same
    patch content across Mesa releases while Mesa keeps editing the file
    the patch touches.

0.4.0
  - Mesa is built at the base image's Mesa version with the base image's OGC
    patches, instead of a pinned pristine tarball.
  - DirectMesh v1.3.1 replaces the old RADV_GFX103 mesh-shader approach.
  - The maintained FSR4 series (0003-0007) is included.
